	regionKind = "dungeon",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Stockade is the prison of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. It lies beneath the city, behind a grim gate beside the canals near the {link:mage-quarter}Mage Quarter{/link}. Its cells hold the worst criminals of the kingdom: murderers, rebels, Dark Iron raiders and, above all, the captured men of the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}. For years it was the quiet answer to every disorder in the realm. Now it is a disorder of its own. The prisoners have risen, driven out their guards and taken the cellblocks for themselves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records when the Stockade was built, nor who first kept its keys. As the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} grew bolder in {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} and {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, more and more of its cells filled with men in red bandanas.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The riot began among the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} prisoners and spread through every block. {link:warden-thelwater}Warden Thelwater{/link} and his guards now hold only the entrance. Inside, the inmates rule the halls, and the most dangerous among them have made the cells their fortresses. At their head stands {link:bazil-thredd}Bazil Thredd{/link}, one of {link:edwin-vancleef}Edwin VanCleef{/link}'s lieutenants. Thredd did not rise alone. Before the riot he received a visitor from outside the walls, and the trail of that visitor leads toward {link:stormwind-keep}Stormwind Keep{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inmates",
			text = [=[• {b}{link:bazil-thredd}Bazil Thredd{/link}.{/b} The {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} lieutenant who leads the uprising.
• {b}{link:targorr-the-dread}Targorr the Dread{/link}.{/b} A prisoner whose crimes {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link} has not forgiven.
• {b}{link:kam-deepfury}Kam Deepfury{/link}.{/b} A Dark Iron prisoner wanted by the dwarves of {link:dun-modr}Dun Modr{/link}.
• {b}{link:dextren-ward}Dextren Ward{/link}.{/b} A criminal whose hand the council of {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link} has demanded.
• {b}{link:hamhock}Hamhock{/link}.{/b} An {link:ogres}ogre{/link} of great size and little patience, loose among the cells.
• {b}{link:bruegal-ironknuckle}Bruegal Ironknuckle{/link}.{/b} A rarely seen and much feared prisoner of the deepest blocks.
• {b}The Defias inmates.{/b} Prisoners, convicts, captives and insurgents who now rule the halls.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Prison",
			text = [=[• The towns of the kingdom have long memories. {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link}, {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link} and the dwarves of the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link} each have a prisoner here whom they want to see answer for his crimes.
• The red bandanas of the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias{/link} are worn even in the cells. In {link:old-town}Old Town{/link}, Nikova Raskol has asked for a great many of them.
• The Stockade's riot is not only a matter for the warden. It is the first thread of a plot that leads from the {link:the-deadmines}Deadmines{/link} to {link:stormwind-keep}Stormwind Keep{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

